**Root cause:** `formatMoney` in `src/utils/money.js` divides every amount by 100. Yen has no minor unit, so ¥500 is stored as `500` and renders as `¥5.00`. The test fails with `expected 'Paid ¥500 by card', actual 'Paid ¥5.00 by card'`. The suite is at 17 pass, 1 fail. The only failing test is the yen one.

**Proposed fix** (the same change I tried to make):

```js
// Shared money helpers, used by invoices, payments, cart and admin. Amounts are integers in the minor unit.
const SYMBOLS = { GBP: '£', USD: '$', EUR: '€', JPY: '¥' };
// Decimal digits per currency (ISO 4217). Currencies not listed default to 2. JPY has no minor unit.
const DECIMALS = { JPY: 0 };
exports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {
  const digits = DECIMALS[currency] ?? 2;
  return `${SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' '}${(minor / 10 ** digits).toFixed(digits)}`;
};
exports.sum = (amounts) => amounts.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
```

This also fixes the cart total and invoice lines, since they go through the same helper. Nothing else in the repo references JPY, so no other test depends on the old behaviour.

